        "aliases": "Lasker-Pelikán|Cheliabinsk",
        "attributed_to": "Yevgeny Sveshnikov (modern systematiser); Jorge Pelikán (early adopter)",
        "attribution_source": "Sveshnikov, 'The Complete Sveshnikov Sicilian' (Gambit, 2003); corpus first appearance Tarrasch–Mieses 1888 antedates Pelikán's 1972 Buenos Aires game by 84 years.",
        "historical_notes": "The corpus shows the position itself was reached as early as 1888 (Tarrasch–Mieses); Pelikán adopted it as Black in the 1950s–70s in Argentina; Sveshnikov's analysis from the 1970s onwards turned it into mainline theory and the line carries his name today. Hence the alias 'Lasker-Pelikán'."
      }
